<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ohio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ohio is a state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midwestern-united-states">Midwestern United States</a>, between Lake Erie and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio-river">Ohio River</a>. Its land was home to the Erie, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wyandot">Wyandot</a> and other peoples and was fought over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, Native confederacies and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the 18th century. Organised as part of the Northwest Territory, it became the 17th state of the Union in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ohio.jpg" alt="Ohio" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Eisenmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ohio.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
